/** \page coretypes Core Types

@section CoreTypes_ByteOrder Converting Byte Orders

The byteorder conversion API consists of two sets of functions. The Pt::swab
function is able to swap the byteorder of a type by bytewise copying as shown
in the following example:

@code
Pt::uint32_t value = ...;
Pt::uint32_t swapped = Pt::swab(value);
@endcode

The swab function is overloaded for all fixed-size integer types such as
%Pt::uint32_t. A second set of functions can be used to convert from a specific
external byteorder to the native host byteorder:

- Pt::beToHost
- Pt::hostToBe
- Pt::leToHost
- Pt::hostToLe

For example the function beToHost converts from big-endian to the host byte
order:

@code
Pt::uint32_t beVal = readBigEndian();
Pt::uint32_t value = Pt::beToHost(beVal);
@endcode

*/
